cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Essaim OS"
message: "If you reference Essaim OS, its hardware documentation, or its Linux hardware drivers, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Essaim OS"
    website: "https://essaimos.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ESSAIM-OS/essaim-docs"
url: "https://essaimos.com"
abstract: >-
  Essaim OS is a self-hosted, local-LAN GPU, CPU, and Solo ASIC cryptocurrency
  mining operating system and fleet orchestrator written in Rust. It runs on
  Raspberry Pi, Docker, bare-metal Linux USB sticks, Proxmox/QEMU VMs, and
  Windows WSL2 with zero cloud dependency, live GPU auto-tuning, global smart
  electricity tariff automation (EDF Tempo, Octopus Agile, PVPC, aWATTar,
  Tibber, TOU), local-LAN Shelly Gen1-Gen4 smart plug energy metering and power
  control, and native Linux hardware RGB, cooler display, and AIO control.
